{"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Retained history, checkpoints and resources","modules":[{"name":"UndoKit"}]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Topics","identifiers":["doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HistoryReading","doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HistoryRetentionManaging","doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HistoryRecoveryPlan","doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HistoryStore"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Browsing retained History does not move ordinary Undo\/Redo position."}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Read-narrowly","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Read narrowly"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Give browsers ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HistoryReading","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and policy owners ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HistoryRetentionManaging","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Metadata pages do not decode every state. A Checkpoint is a host-designated opaque","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"state reference; the host owns semantic completeness and required dependencies.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A new edit after Undo can retire ordinary Redo eligibility while retaining the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displaced continuation’s history.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HistoryRecoveryPlan","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to obtain a coherent bounded sequence of opaque","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"accepted-effect transitions. Release the plan when complete or cancelled. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"host retrieves required codecs\/resources, reconstructs an isolated state and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"validates it. Reading or reconstruction does not restore live content. To adopt","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the result, submit a new Command carrying its restoration origin.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Protect-what-recovery-needs","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Protect what recovery needs"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"State protection and detailed-history protection are distinct promises. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Checkpoint or state hold preserves state dependencies; a detailed hold can retain","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the transition material needed for further browsing\/reconstruction. Resource","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"references identify host-owned bytes; UndoKit does not copy or interpret their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"meaning. Preserve required host codecs and resources while retained history,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"active plans or pending work can still reference them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Run bounded retention\/consolidation maintenance under the selected host policy.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Whole Undo Groups must remain coherent; ordinary depth is not a count of individual","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"members. Physical resource cleanup belongs to the store-wide fence because other","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scopes can retain the same host objects. Do not infer that loss of Undo availability","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"permits deleting retained History or shared resources.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Recording-and-continuity","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Recording and continuity"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Recording-Off changes are undoable in the open session, but the first accepted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Off change creates a gap that cannot be crossed to older ordinary Actions.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Re-enabling recording adopts a coherent host baseline. Earlier retained states","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"may still be read under their existing codec\/resource requirements.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Clearing settled history establishes a new generation. A quarantined unresolved","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reset requires independent knowledge of current domain state and an explicit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"host decision; it is not ordinary error handling. Delayed requests bound to a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retired generation must be refused before delivery.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/undokit\/retainedhistoryandresources"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/RetainedHistoryAndResources","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit"],["doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit","doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/RecoveryAndStorage"],["doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit","doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/AppKitIntegration","doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/RecoveryAndStorage"],["doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit","doc:\/\/dev.foliosuite.UndoKit\/documentation\/UndoKit\/HostingYourModel","doc:\/\/de